<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $273.7 mln April 15.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $273.7 mln April 15.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $273.7 million surplus on April 15 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 15</p>
<p>Exports: $252.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $223 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $464.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $220.8 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $273.7 million</p>
<p>ARPIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.296 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.246 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.265 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.760 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $555 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
